.SH NAME
md_frontend_2node__modules_2date-fns_2docs_2unicode_tokens \- Unicode Tokens 
.PP


.PP
Starting with v2, \fRformat\fP and \fRparse\fP use \fRUnicode tokens\fP\&.

.PP
The tokens are different from Moment\&.js and other libraries that opted to use custom formatting rules\&. While usage of a standard ensures compatibility and the future of the library, it causes confusion that this document intends to resolve\&.
.SH "Popular mistakes"
.PP
There are 4 tokens that cause most of the confusion:

.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRD\fP and \fRDD\fP that represent the day of a year (1, 2, \&.\&.\&., 365, 366) are often confused with \fRd\fP and \fRdd\fP that represent the day of a month (1, 2, \&.\&.\&., 31)\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRYY\fP and \fRYYYY\fP that represent the local week-numbering year (44, 01, 00, 17) are often confused with \fRyy\fP and \fRyyyy\fP that represent the calendar year\&.
.PP

.PP
.PP
.nf
// ❌ Wrong!
format(new Date(), "YYYY\-MM\-DD");
//=> 2018\-10\-283

// ✅ Correct
format(new Date(), "yyyy\-MM\-dd");
//=> 2018\-10\-10

// ❌ Wrong!
parse("11\&.02\&.87", "D\&.MM\&.YY", new Date())\&.toString();
//=> 'Sat Jan 11 1986 00:00:00 GMT+0200 (EET)'

// ✅ Correct
parse("11\&.02\&.87", "d\&.MM\&.yy", new Date())\&.toString();
//=> 'Wed Feb 11 1987 00:00:00 GMT+0200 (EET)'
.fi
.PP

.PP
To help with the issue, \fRformat\fP and \fRparse\fP functions won't accept these tokens without \fRuseAdditionalDayOfYearTokens\fP option for \fRD\fP and \fRDD\fP and \fRuseAdditionalWeekYearTokens\fP options for \fRYY\fP and \fRYYYY\fP:

.PP
.PP
.nf
format(new Date(), "D", { useAdditionalDayOfYearTokens: true });
//=> '283'

parse("365+1987", "DD+YYYY", new Date(), {
  useAdditionalDayOfYearTokens: true,
  useAdditionalWeekYearTokens: true,
})\&.toString();
//=> 'Wed Dec 31 1986 00:00:00 GMT+0200 (EET)'
.fi
.PP
 
